# HunyuanOCR 1B + its matching projector, both from the first-party ggml-org
# conversion. bf16 on a 1B model costs ~2 GiB and avoids quantisation damage on
# dense glyphs. Temperature 0: OCR is transcription, not generation.
SIDECAR_PORT=8083
SIDECAR_ALIAS=hunyuan-ocr
SIDECAR_MODEL=/home/typhoon/git/frankenstein-llm/models/ocr/HunyuanOCR-bf16.gguf
SIDECAR_DEVICE=ROCm0,ROCm1,ROCm2
SIDECAR_NGL=all
SIDECAR_CTX=16384
SIDECAR_BATCH=2048
SIDECAR_UBATCH=2048
# Placement: one card. 3,6,2 was the pre-2026-09-06 catalog default and gave the
# throttling V620 the majority of the layers of a model that fits on a single
# 6900 XT. llama-models.ini stopped using it in f2576ac; this file was not
# updated with it. Layer split is pipelined, so every token crossed two extra
# devices for no capacity reason. Measured on kernel 7.2.3-273-tkg-eevdf-llvm,
# sized by scripts/gpu_placement.py --scan at 4.01 GiB, which fits ROCm0 alone.
SIDECAR_EXTRA_ARGS=--mmproj /home/typhoon/git/frankenstein-llm/models/ocr/mmproj-HunyuanOCR-bf16.gguf --temp 0 --flash-attn off --cache-type-v f16 --tensor-split 1,0,0
